<template>
    <SiteShell page="features">
        <div class="page-head">
            <span class="kicker">Capability sheet</span>
            <h1>Features</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                The authoring surface is small on purpose: typed items, one scene
                IR and one render pipeline. Everything below is implemented in
                the DSL or the native binding today.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Authoring DSL <span class="tag">TypeScript</span></h2>
            <ul>
                <li><code>Film</code> sets canvas size, design cards and audio, then collects scenes.</li>
                <li>
                    <code>Scene</code> holds timed items: <code>text</code>,
                    <code>code</code>, <code>counter</code>, <code>shape</code>,
                    <code>image</code>, <code>video</code>, <code>chart</code>,
                    <code>callout</code>, <code>path</code>, <code>layer</code> and
                    <code>instance</code>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Layout helpers include <code>card</code>, <code>footnote</code>,
                    <code>progress</code>, <code>bands</code>, <code>glow</code> and
                    <code>grain</code>.
                </li>
                <li>Items are plain values, so films compose with ordinary functions, loops and data.</li>
                <li>Timing is written in seconds; the binding converts to frames.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Time and motion</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Every animated item gets an <code>id</code>, an <code>anim</code> window and optional <code>follow</code> timing.</li>
                <li>Evaluation happens in the shared <code>media.motion</code> stage, not in the authoring code.</li>
                <li>Entrances and exits are expressed as time windows, so a scene stays a single serializable value.</li>
                <li>
                    Only motion fields are animated. Arbitrary property curves
                    are not supported, and the roadmap says so instead of
                    pretending otherwise.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Sound as code</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Eight effect families: whoosh, impact, riser, tick, glitch, sub, ambience and sparkle.</li>
                <li>Seventeen instruments — nine drums and eight melodic voices — addressed by MIDI note.</li>
                <li>Eight drum grooves, or sixteen step velocities per bar when a preset is not enough.</li>
                <li>
                    Singing is synthesized from five vowels and an onset class;
                    the same song and seed stay byte-identical.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Narration is a reserved slot for a PCM16 WAV you supply, not
                    a generator.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Design tokens</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Semantic color roles are declared with <code>colorToken('ink')</code> and friends.</li>
                <li>A project design card sets the defaults; a scene card overrides individual roles.</li>
                <li>A role marked <code>locked</code> cannot be overridden — the mismatch is an explicit error, never a silent priority.</li>
                <li>Unknown roles, duplicate roles and non-color values fail with the structural path.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Media and preflight</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Images are decoded through WIC; video frames and audio come through a Media Foundation source reader, cached per path.</li>
                <li><code>fit</code> selects <code>contain</code>, <code>cover</code> or <code>stretch</code>; <code>radius</code> clips to rounded corners.</li>
                <li><code>srcIn</code> starts a clip at a chosen source frame instead of the beginning.</li>
                <li>
                    Required sources are checked before the encoder opens. A
                    missing or undecodable asset aborts with a located error;
                    intentional empty slots are declared with
                    <code>required: false</code>.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Reproducible runs</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><code>open-cut build</code> prints the native version, the exact source revision and whether the tree was dirty.</li>
                <li><code>RenderStats</code> reports the frame range, fonts actually loaded, a project hash and empty optional slots.</li>
                <li><code>--from</code> and <code>--to</code> export an interval renumbered from zero.</li>
                <li><code>--cancel-file</code> stops between frames and keeps the previous output intact.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Platform honesty</h2>
            <p>
                Prebuilt natives exist for Windows x64, Linux x64/arm64 and macOS
                x64/arm64. MP4 encoding runs through Windows Media Foundation, so
                the complete render chain needs Windows; N/KN editions require
                the Media Feature Pack. The audio codec is negotiated: AAC is
                preferred and the encoder falls back to FLAC when no AAC encoder
                is registered.
            </p>
            <p>
                Not supported today: scene transitions (cuts are hard), multitrack
                compositing (items paint in list order, scene by scene), narration
                synthesis, arbitrary property curves, and WASM or browser
                execution.
            </p>
        </section>

        <p class="cta-line">
            Wondering how the pieces connect?
            <Link to="WorkflowPage">
                Follow the render pipeline
            </Link>
        </p>
    </SiteShell>
</template>

